From eeb3ee655d89febd10262fec754101e5ad5f27df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YahiaAngelo <yahia.mostafa.elsayed@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:40:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] cputlb: keep global TLB entries across ASID switches
 (VPHONE_ASID_NG); event-rate counters

An ASID switch (TTBR0/1_EL1 write) flushed every MMU index. Architecturally it
only invalidates non-global (nG) translations, and QEMU's TLB holds only the
current ASID's, so now:

- ptw records nG in CPUTLBEntryFull.vphone_ng (two-range regimes);
- each MMU index logs the slots filled with nG entries (up to 2048; beyond
  that the next switch flushes the index);
- tlb_flush_asid_switch() drops only those (and nG victims) in the EL1&0
  indexes (E10_0, E10_1, E10_1_PAN, GE10_1, GE10_1_PAN), leaves the physical
  and stage-2 indexes alone, and flushes the rest;
- a range flush too long to do page by page, wholly below bit 63, in an index
  with no global entries there, drops the logged entries that overlap it
  (whole blocks, by lg_page_size) instead of the whole index.

VPHONE_ASID_NG=0 restores the old full flush.

iPhone Duo (iOS 27.1), per second: TLB fills during boot 4.3M -> 2.2-2.4M,
app launches 3.7M -> 1.9-2.1M (kernel upper-half refills -65..85%, physical
index refills -80%); range flushes escalated to whole-index flushes 6.9k ->
0.9k at boot. MMU walk + fill share of vCPU time 11-17% -> ~9%. guestbench,
3 boots x 5 runs per arm: median 5.17 s vs 5.45 s (within boot-to-boot noise).

Diagnostics (off by default): VPHONE_EVENT_STATS=<seconds> logs per-second
rates of exceptions by kind, GENTER/GEXIT/ERET, TLB fills (per MMU index and
address half), flushes by kind and escalation, SPRR/GXF flush sources, ASID
reuse, translations (and their cycles), MMIO and code-page writes
(include/qemu/vphone-ev.h, util/vphone-ev.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N89PWg24VJrcxX3MuUo4uM
